      "explanation": "Sensitivity uses everyone confirmed to have the infection as the denominator. The new test detected 22 of the 45 true cases, so sensitivity = 22 ÷ 45 × 100 = 48.9%, about 49%. The four positive results among uninfected people are false positives and do not enter this calculation.",
