      "basis": "concept",
      "explanation": "A zero-millimeter skin test soon after exposure can be falsely negative. Follow-up testing is usually timed eight to ten weeks after the last exposure, and assessment for active disease comes first. The stem gives neither the exposure date nor risk factors that determine preventive treatment, so its fixed four-week repeat rule is not a reliable universal answer.",
