      "explanation": "Sensitivity = true positives / all confirmed diseased people = 22 / 45 × 100 = 48.9%. C (48%) is the closest listed choice, although 49% would be the proper whole-number rounding. The two negative tests among PCR-negative people are not part of this denominator.",
