      "basis": "concept",
      "explanation": "Case management detects and treats malaria after infection has occurred, so it is the secondary-prevention choice. Chemoprophylaxis and larval control aim to prevent new disease and are primary measures. The level depends on timing, not simply on whether an intervention reduces transmission.",
