      "confidence": "supported",
      "basis": "lecture",
      "explanation": "Positive predictive value asks how many positive mammograms represent true disease. Of 136 positive results, 126 are true positives, so PPV = 126 / (126 + 10) × 100 = 92.6%. The single false negative belongs in the sensitivity calculation, not this denominator.",
      "objection": "",
